<title>PAKISTAN: Pakistan cotton output reaches 8.78 million bales.</title>
<headline>Pakistan cotton output reaches 8.78 million bales.</headline>
<dateline>KARACHI, Pakistan 1997-06-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pakistan's cotton output from the 1996/97 (July-June) crop reached a provisional 8.78 million 375-lb bales by June 15, down from 9.938 million bales at the same time a year ago, the Pakistan Cotton Ginners Association said on Thursday.</p>
<p>Delivery and ginning figures in million bales from Punjab and Sindh provinces (year-ago figures in brackets):</p>
<p>		    Punjab	   Sindh	    Total</p>
<p> Delivery	 6.696 (8.167)  2.087 (1.771)  8.783 (9.938)</p>
<p> Pressed	  6.694 (8.166)  2.087 (1.769)  8.782 (9.935)</p>
<p> Mill sales     6.394 (7.021)  2.050 (1.297)  8.445 (8.318)</p>
<p> Export sales   0.033 (0.949)  0.006 (0.441)  0.039 (1.390)</p>
<p> CEC		nil   (nil)    nil   (nil)    nil   (nil)</p>
<p> Unsold	   0.267 (0.195)  0.030 (0.030)  0.297 (0.225)</p>
<p>-- Karachi newsroom 9221-5685192</p>
</text>
